<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Catherine the Great</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1729">1729</a>–<a href="/years/1796">1796</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Catherine II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Catherine the Great, or Catherine II, was empress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> from 1762 to 1796. Her reign saw major territorial expansion, including gains on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. She took part in the three partitions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>, which erased it from the map, and her rule is regarded as a high point of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>'s power and Enlightenment-influenced government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great.jpg" alt="Catherine the Great" width="320" height="381" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: After Alexander Roslin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Catherine_II_after_Roslin,_Rokotov_(1780s,_Kunsthistorisches_Museum).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
